---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Mike Kelley | Technical Writing & Documentation Engineering" description="Technical writer and documentation leader with 15+ years across software, APIs, cybersecurity, aviation, and complex manufacturing. Documentation engineering, docs-as-code, and team leadership.">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">TECHNICAL WRITING · DOCUMENTATION ENGINEERING · LEADERSHIP</p>
    <h1>Making complex systems easier to understand</h1>
    <p class="lede">I’m a technical writer and documentation lead with more than 15 years of experience explaining software, APIs, cybersecurity systems, aviation requirements, and complex manufacturing processes. I bring together clear writing, technical curiosity, practical tooling, and the judgment to make documentation work for the people who rely on it.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href={`${base}writing/`}>Explore writing samples</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}resume/`}>View career history</a>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-row">
      <div><strong>15+ years</strong><span>technical documentation</span></div>
      <div><strong>Docs-as-code</strong><span>Git, Markdown, Sphinx, Jekyll</span></div>
      <div><strong>Hands-on</strong><span>HTML, CSS, JavaScript, APIs</span></div>
      <div><strong>AI-assisted workflows</strong><span>Prompting, implementation, review</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="strengths">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">WHAT I BRING</p>
      <h2>Strong content, sound engineering, reliable delivery</h2>
      <p>My work spans more than writing pages. I learn how a system works, identify what its audience needs to do, and build documentation and workflows that stay useful as the product changes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="project-grid">
      <a class="project-card" href={`${base}writing/`}>
        <span class="tag">01 · Content</span>
        <h3>Technical writing and information design</h3>
        <p>Task-focused instructions, API and developer documentation, reference content, troubleshooting, and explanations for both technical and nontechnical audiences.</p>
        <span class="text-link">Writing samples ↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="project-card" href={`${base}docs-as-code/`}>
        <span class="tag">02 · Engineering</span>
        <h3>Documentation systems and docs-as-code</h3>
        <p>SaltStack’s Sphinx/LaTeX-to-Jekyll/PrinceXML migration, pull-request-driven CI/CD builds, and this site’s automated Astro-to-GitHub Pages deployment.</p>
        <span class="text-link">Explore the workflow ↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="project-card" href={`${base}demos/`}>
        <span class="tag">03 · Implementation</span>
        <h3>Code, APIs, and interactive demos</h3>
        <p>Working examples of API integration, asynchronous JavaScript, form validation, responsive layouts, and accessible interface behavior.</p>
        <span class="text-link">Try the demos ↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">TECHNICAL RANGE</p>
        <h2>Comfortable with content and code</h2>
        <p>I’ve worked with developers and subject-matter experts to document systems where accuracy matters, from API behavior and cybersecurity concepts to aviation regulatory content and complex manufacturing programs. I can work directly with source files and tooling, not just a word processor.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="resume-list">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Authoring and publishing</strong><span>MadCap Flare, Markdown, Sphinx, Jekyll, XML, HTML, CSS, and PDF/HTML output.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Developer workflows</strong><span>Git from the command line, API documentation, Python docstrings and type hints, JavaScript, and build pipelines.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Quality and usability</strong><span>Content standards, validation, troubleshooting, review workflows, and audience-centered information design.</span></li>
          <li><strong>AI-assisted workflows</strong><span>Use AI tools to investigate technical problems, make targeted changes in an existing codebase, and keep documentation aligned with implementation. I document the trade-offs and review AI-generated changes rather than treating them as automatically correct. See the <a href={`${base}demos/`}>OpenWeather API demo</a> for a practical example.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">LEADERSHIP AND COLLABORATION</p>
      <h2>Helping teams deliver accurate work</h2>
      <p>I’ve led documentation teams and previously supervised up to 19 QA technicians supporting HP testing. I’ve supported quality-focused work where deadlines, traceability, and details matter. My approach is to make priorities clear, build repeatable processes, coach people through difficult work, and work across Engineering, Quality, Manufacturing, and Program Management to resolve issues before they become delivery problems.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="check-grid">
      <p><strong>Planning and prioritization</strong><br />Balance capacity, dependencies, due dates, and competing program needs.</p>
      <p><strong>Standards and process</strong><br />Create usable guidelines, consistent workflows, and clearer review expectations.</p>
      <p><strong>Coaching and development</strong><br />Help teammates build skills, take ownership, and improve the quality of their work.</p>
      <p><strong>Continuous improvement</strong><br />Use recurring issues and feedback to improve both the process and the finished documentation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap contact-inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">EXPLORE THE PORTFOLIO</p>
        <h2>Work examples beyond the skills list</h2>
        <p>Browse writing samples, see how documentation can fit into an engineering workflow, try the interactive examples, or review my career history.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="contact-links">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}writing/`}>Writing samples</a>
        <a href={`${base}docs-as-code/`}>Docs-as-code ↗</a>
        <a href={`${base}demos/`}>Interactive code demos ↗</a>
        <a href={`${base}resume/`}>Resume and career history ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
